  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Smt. K Sravani vs Sri. K.Srisailam on 4 July, 2024 Author: P.Sree Sudha Bench: P.Sree Sudha The Hon'Ble Smt.Justice P.Sree Sudha Transfer Civil Miscellaneous Petition No.136 of 2024 Order: Smt. K Sravani vs Sri. K.Srisailam on 4 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/186177920/ 1 6.",
    "facts": "It came to know that petitioner affected with cancer in September, 2023. It is further stated that respondent-husband dropped petitioner at her parents house and could not take care of her and he filed O.P for divorce vide F.C.O.P.No.17 of 2024 but petitioner intended to take steps for Restitution of Conjugal Rights vide F.C.O.P(SR) No.801 of 2022 and also filed M.C.No.105 of 2022.",
    "arguments": "It was further contended that petitioner is financially week and suffering from Cancer and thus requested for transfer of Divorce O.P filed by her husband. 3. It is contended by learned counsel for the respondent that on 12.07.2023 respondent took the petitioner to the Hospital then the petitioner left the hospital with her mother without intimating him. It was further stated that medical record also placed on record. 4. Learned counsel for the petitioner relied upon citation reported in \"Anuradha Samir Vennangot vs. Mohandas Samir Vennangot\" 1 in which it was held that: \"Wife suffering from life-threatening disease-pre existing obligation of husband to care for wife in sickness. It cannot be disputed that after marriage, law enjoins the corresponding duty on the husband to look after her comforts and not only to provide her food and clothes but to protect her from all calamities and to take care of her health and safety.\" 5."
  },
